---
/* The site's arrow, the one arrow everywhere (after Foster + Partners'):
   a bold stem down from the top that turns at a right angle and runs on to
   an open head, the turn and the head's point sharp, the ends cut square.
   Drawn on a 24 square in currentColor, its stroke a tenth of the square, so
   it is the same weight at any size and takes the colour of where it stands.
   Its size, colour and movement are each place's own (style.css, by the
   class it is given), as before; it only ever reads the same.

   Its base points right, on along the line: forward, next, open, go. Turned
   another way: `flip` mirrors it to point left (back, previous), `rotate`
   turns it by so many degrees. Both are set as the separate `scale` and
   `rotate` properties, not `transform`, so a place's own movement
   (a nudge on hover, button.js's step) still moves it as before. A place
   that turns its arrow from its stylesheet (a previous button) does the
   same, with `scale` or `rotate`.

   One other shape, the floating menu's (FloatingNav.astro), also on the
   Architecture row's arrows, turned to point left and right: `corner`,
   the menu cards' own arrow kept, an open head whose arms run along the
   top and the right of the square and a shaft from its point most of the
   way to the opposite corner, drawn the same way as the site's arrow (the
   same square, square ends and sharp corners), a little smaller within its
   square and a little heavier, so it holds its own at the menu's small
   size.

   And `straight`: a plain arrow, a level shaft to an open head, drawn the
   same way (the home hero's Learn more). */
interface Props {
  class?: string;
  flip?: boolean;
  rotate?: number;
  shape?: 'turn' | 'corner' | 'straight';
}
const { class: className, flip = false, rotate = 0, shape = 'turn' } = Astro.props;
const style = [flip && 'scale: -1 1', rotate && `rotate: ${rotate}deg`].filter(Boolean).join('; ') || undefined;
// Each shape's path and stroke, on the 24 square
const SHAPES = {
  turn: { d: 'M5 3V15H17.6M14 10L19 15L14 20', weight: 2.4 },
  corner: { d: 'M6 4.5H19.5V18M19.5 4.5L5.5 18.5', weight: 3.2 },
  straight: { d: 'M3.5 12H19.5M13.5 6L19.5 12L13.5 18', weight: 2.4 },
};
const { d, weight } = SHAPES[shape];
---
<svg class:list={['arrow', className]} style={style} viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d={d} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width={weight} stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter"/></svg>
